+---
+id: task-003-ten-percent-off-rentals-of-three-days-or-more
+type: task
+title: "Ten percent off rentals of three days or more"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Request
+
+A rental of 3 days or more now costs 10% less than its full price. Quotes and bookings both show the
+reduced total. The request is to reward customers who stay longer.
+
+# Work
+
+- Tests first, in `src/rental.test.ts`: the existing three-day quote test moved to two days, since it
+  asserted the full price; new tests for a two-day rental (no discount), a three-day and a seven-day
+  rental (10% off), rounding to the cent with halves up, `book` charging the discounted total, and
+  `book` and `quote` agreeing. Run before the implementation, the three discount tests failed.
+- Implementation in `src/rental.ts`: `priceOf`, which both `quote` and `book` use, applies the discount
+  when the period is three days or more. The discount is computed in integer arithmetic.
+- `src/rental.ts` interface doc comments for `quote` and `book`, and `README.md`, describe the discount.
+- The rounding choice is recorded in dl-005.
+
+# Result
+
+- `npm test` builds with strict TypeScript and runs 32 tests, all passing: the 27 existing tests, with
+  one changed to a two-day period, and 5 new ones.
+- Not changed: `availability` and `addEquipment`. Their behaviour is as before.
+- Not decided: whether a discount should show as a separate line with the full price. Quotes and
+  bookings show only the total, as they did before.
